 "title": "HexOct: Knitting Crystals: the edge-on slice of every close-packed stacking as a knitted pattern",
 "description": "<p><b>Withdrawn for revision.</b> Versions 1 and 2 knitted an edge-on slice of the close-packed stackings, a picture of the crystal on a flat fabric. DICTO proposed a fabric that is the crystal: one continuous multi-layer knitted fabric whose sheets are the close-packed layers and whose linking yarns, carrying c and h, make the HexOct tiles the knitted cells through its thickness. That fabric is in preparation and will be published as the next version of this record, under the same DOI.</p>",
